@theme leaving
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.
// Beat 3: they stay (a real transfer needs the rotation; social's Part 8b handles any real goodbye).

== beat 1
tone: light
hint: Just reading the board. The other board. The transfer list. Idle curiosity.
mem: list
them: Just reading the transfer list. Idle curiosity. Very idle. Barely curious.   [laugh]
them: There's a posting on a station with a park. A real park. With grass.
? choice
* Grass? Tempting.   flavour:cheer
  them: Isn't it? You could lie on it. I'd forgotten you could lie on things.
* Thinking of going?   flavour:listen mem:asked
  them: Me? No. Probably not. I don't know. I'm reading, that's all.
them: Anyway. Grass. Imagine.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: Can I think out loud at you? I've got a decision and it won't sit still.
mem: decide
them: I've got an offer. A real one, off that list. They want an answer by the end of the month.   [sigh]
them: Part of me wants something new. Part of me can't picture my days without this lot.
them: I don't know which part is me and which part is just tired.
? choice
* What would you miss most, if you went?   flavour:listen mem:miss
  them: The people. The hum. Even the queue for the booths. That's a long list, isn't it.
  + them: That's the question, isn't it. The people. You. I'd miss you. That's an answer, sort of.
* Write two lists. Go and stay. See which is longer.   flavour:practical mem:lists
  them: Lists. Yes. I'm good at lists. Better than at deciding.
* I'd miss you. For what it's worth.   flavour:share mem:wouldmiss
  them: It's worth a lot. More than you'd think.
them: Thanks. No answer yet. But it's quieter in my head.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: I've decided. Come here. You get to hear first.
mem: staying
them: I turned it down. The post with the park. I wrote back this morning.
them: I made the two lists. The "stay" one was longer. It had more names on it.   [laugh]
them: The grass will still be there one day. This lot won't always be. I want to be here for it.
? choice
* I'm really glad.   flavour:listen
  them: Me too. It's a good ship. It's a good ship with good people.
  + them: Me too. Your name was on the list, you know. Near the top.
* The park's loss.   flavour:cheer
  them: Ha. The park will cope. It's got grass. It's fine.   [laugh]
them: Right. Back to it. Staying. It feels good to say.
